# ============================================================
# AD-3D-CNN repository ignore rules
# ============================================================

# --- Python runtime caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Occlusion sub-experiment working directory ---
# Set by work_dir in occlusion/occlusion_config.py (the occlusion node of config.yaml) or by the
# AD3DCNN_OCC_WORK environment variable; masks/ results/ figures/ all live under it.
# It is deliberately **NOT** ignored: as documented in occlusion/README.md §4.2, its results/
# subdirectory ships the *frozen inputs* that the CPU statistics chain reads, so the chain runs
# out of the box. Re-running that chain overwrites those files — the same convention as
# results/ and reference_results/, which are tracked and also get overwritten by re-runs
# (see results/README.md §5). occlusion/reference_results/ remains the authoritative archive.

# --- Runtime output of the evaluation / preprocessing scripts ---
# Note: results/gradcam_aggregate_v3/per_sample_results_final.csv is an input to the occlusion
#       sub-experiment, so results/ is not ignored as a whole — only the usual temporary files.
*.tmp
*.log.tmp

# Training runtime artifacts: every grid search / smoke test creates a new Grid_SEARCH_*
# directory (checkpoints and TensorBoard events; a single one can reach hundreds of MB), which
# must not enter the repository.
results/Grid_SEARCH_*/
events.out.tfevents.*
# Temporary output directories of evaluate/ and figures/. An early revision also carried an
# ignore rule for a Chinese-named temporary directory produced by the scripts of that time;
# the translated scripts now write English paths only, so that legacy rule has been dropped.
figures/output/

# --- Virtual environments / tool caches ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Operating-system clutter ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
